## 📊 Dataset

This project uses the IBM Telco Customer Churn dataset.

### Dataset Summary

| Metric | Value |
|---|---:|
| Total Customers | 7,043 |
| Customers Who Churned | 1,869 |
| Customers Who Did Not Churn | 5,174 |
| Overall Churn Rate | 26.54% |

The dataset contains customer information such as:

- Customer demographics.
- Tenure and account information.
- Contract types.
- Internet and additional services.
- Monthly charges and total charges.
- Customer churn status.

## 🔎 Exploratory Data Analysis

Exploratory data analysis was performed to identify patterns and relationships associated with customer churn.

### Key Analytical Insights

- **Contract Type:** Month-to-month customers exhibit higher churn rates than customers with longer-term contracts.
- **Customer Tenure:** Customers with shorter tenure tend to have higher churn rates.
- **Internet Service:** Fiber optic customers have a higher observed churn rate than DSL customers in this dataset.
- **Retention Opportunities:** Customers with elevated churn risk can be prioritized for targeted retention campaigns.

These findings describe observed patterns in the dataset and do not necessarily establish causation.

### EDA Visualizations

The project includes visualizations analyzing:

- Churn by contract type.
- Churn by internet service.
- Churn by customer tenure.
- Monthly charges by churn status.

## 🤖 Machine Learning Model

An XGBoost classification pipeline was trained to predict customer churn.

The model development process includes:

1. Data preprocessing.
2. Feature engineering.
3. Training and testing data preparation.
4. Model training.
5. Performance evaluation.
6. Model explainability.

### Model Performance

| Evaluation Metric | Score |
|---|---:|
| Accuracy | 79.42% |
| Precision | 64.38% |
| Recall | 50.27% |
| F1-Score | 56.46% |
| ROC-AUC | 83.66% |

The ROC-AUC score indicates that the model can distinguish between customers who churn and those who do not reasonably well.

The recall score also highlights an opportunity to improve the identification of customers who eventually churn.

## 🧠 Explainable AI

SHAP (SHapley Additive exPlanations) is used to help interpret model predictions and understand how features contribute to the model's output.

### Explainability Outputs

- SHAP summary plot.
- SHAP feature importance plot.

These visualizations help communicate the factors influencing model predictions.

## 💰 Revenue Intelligence

The revenue intelligence component estimates potential revenue exposure and categorizes customers into high-, medium-, and low-risk groups.

### Revenue Risk Summary

| Indicator | Result |
|---|---:|
| High-Risk Customers | 730 |
| Medium-Risk Customers | 1,292 |
| Low-Risk Customers | 5,021 |
| Estimated Monthly Revenue Exposure | $139,030.10 |
| Estimated Annual Revenue Exposure | $1,668,361.17 |

### Business Value

- Identify customers who may require immediate retention attention.
- Prioritize retention campaigns based on customer risk.
- Understand potential revenue exposure.
- Support customer retention planning with data-driven insights.

> **Important:** Revenue exposure is an estimate based on the project's methodology. It should not be interpreted as confirmed revenue loss, a calibrated probability of financial loss, or guaranteed savings.

## 📈 Power BI Dashboard

The interactive Power BI dashboard presents customer churn patterns, revenue exposure, and retention priorities in a consolidated business intelligence report.

### Dashboard Features

- Overall customer churn rate.
- Estimated monthly revenue exposure.
- Estimated annual revenue exposure.
- Customer churn by contract type.
- Customer distribution by churn risk.
- Customer retention priority analysis.
- Customer distribution by internet service.
- Contract type filtering.

### Dashboard Preview

